# Cron alternative to the systemd unit/timer pair in this directory.
# NOT installed -- this is a template. Copy the line you want into your own
# crontab (`crontab -e`) after editing the path, and only once you actually
# want scheduling live. See ../docs/SCHEDULING.md.

# MAILTO turns cron's own "command produced output or exited nonzero" mail
# into the cheapest way to have this actually reach a human -- cron will
# email $MAILTO whenever run-batch.sh exits nonzero, which includes exit
# code 2 (a source went silent; see docs/SOURCE_SILENCE_DETECTION.md).
# Requires a working local MTA (sendmail/postfix) on the machine; if you
# don't have one, this line is a no-op and you must rely on the log file
# and/or the admin health API instead.
MAILTO=you@example.com

# Daily at 03:00. Stdout/stderr here duplicate what's already in
# $DATA_DIR/batch.log (the durable, line-buffered record); this redirect is
# only a convenience/backup so `cron`'s own MAILTO has something to attach.
0 3 * * * /CHANGE/ME/mobile-observatory/scheduling/run-batch.sh >> /CHANGE/ME/mobile-observatory/.observatory-data/cron.stdout.log 2>&1
